.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::InterFace\fP< dim >::InitialiseNodeVector ()\fR [protected]\fP"

.PP
connects the nodes of already connected higher dimensional neighbor elements to the \fBInterFace\fP 
.IP "1." 4
From the finite element connected to the Interface we know the topology of the faces of the higher-dimensional neighbor elements so that we can assign their nodes\&. Start with the inside element\&.
.PP

.PP
(We rely on the fact that the nodes on either side of the interface are collocated)

.PP
.IP "2." 4
Find the faces connected to this element and assign them
.IP "3." 4
Get its nodes
.IP "4." 4
Assign the nodes in the same order as for that face since the normal points into the Interface
.IP "5." 4
Repeat for other side
.PP

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
special provisions are made in 1D where there is no corresponding elemnent type for the Interface\&. Thus the number of nodes is assumed to be 1, duplicated to 2\&. 
.RE
.PP

